      "kind": "measurement",
      "request": {
        "description": "Characterize the compiled MuJoCo plant and local 100-step hold margin over a radius-angle grid. For every joint-limit-valid open and folded inverse-kinematic branch, inspect self-contact and roll out matched position, velocity, and combined perturbations under zero input and a bounded local PD controller.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "args": [
              "--artifact",
              "campaigns/evaluations/1ae27a27-6880-4ca6-9d50-e6498e771cb7/plant_margin.json"
            ],
            "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/1ae27a27-6880-4ca6-9d50-e6498e771cb7/plant_margin.json",
            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "startup plant margin and branch characterization",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.plant_margin"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial direction depends on whether failures are likely to be caused by global reach from the reset singularity or by inadequate local stabilization. Compiled mass, damping, actuator, and contact facts constrain that interpretation; paired zero-input versus local-PD retention exposes whether passive dynamics suffice or active velocity shaping is required. Branch- and geometry-conditioned contact records test whether self-contact invalidates the nominal branch model."
      },
